00:16:51,960 --> 00:17:05,400
Dimensional Media Associates Inc., DMA, is a New York City-based technology company that designs, develops, manufactures, and distributes unique floating image 3D volumetric visualization systems.

126
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:10,200
Our clients are an advertising, entertainment, science, medicine, and education.

127
00:17:10,200 --> 00:17:21,800
Founded in 1994 as a partnership and incorporated in June 1996, DMA has positioned itself as a market leader in 3D display technology.

128
00:17:21,800 --> 00:17:40,440
At the heart of DMA's business is a patented breakthrough technology, which DMA developed for producing true 3D aerial images without using lasers and without requiring viewers to wear special eyeglasses or virtual reality headsets or sit in the dark.

129
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:50,080
The full color, full motion images, appear to float in space and can be seen from wide viewing angles under ambient lighting conditions.

130
00:17:50,080 --> 00:17:58,160
3D visualization is the presentation of images in ways that bring out the three-dimensional nature of their content.

131
00:17:58,160 --> 00:18:09,280
Drawings, paintings, and photographs that show perspectives are example of 3D visualization, as are images showing perspective in movies and on television.

132
00:18:09,280 --> 00:18:13,840
Images produced by 3D computer graphics are also examples.

133
00:18:13,840 --> 00:18:21,680
These are all representations of three-dimensional objects, but are themselves actually only two-dimensional.

134
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:38,400
Creation of the illusion that an image is itself three-dimensional can be accomplished with viewing appliances, such as the stereoscopes of previous generations, or the special goggles used to view 3D movies or the headsets used in the creation of virtual reality environments.

135
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:47,120
In general, those devices present slightly different images to the left and right eyes of viewers to achieve the simulation of depth.

136
00:18:47,120 --> 00:18:52,800
Recently, however, a breakthrough technology was created by Dimensional Media Associates Inc.

137
00:18:53,040 --> 00:19:02,800
that actually produces true, three-dimensional images without using lasers and without requiring viewers to wear special appliances.

138
00:19:02,800 --> 00:19:14,080
Further, the full color, full motion images can be seen from wide viewing angles in sizes up to 10 feet and under ambient lighting conditions.

139
00:19:14,080 --> 00:19:34,040
Called high definition volumetric display, HDVD for short, the technology makes use of input from a variety of image generation and storage sources, real-time process data, real objects, television, computer monitors, and flat panel displays.

140
00:19:34,280 --> 00:19:44,760
The projected images appear to float in space and are so real that viewers feel that they can reach out and interact with them.

141
00:19:44,760 --> 00:20:01,400
HDVD uses a complex array of precision optical components, such as parabolic mirrors and beam splitters to collect, focus, and then project light into space to form real volumetric images.

142
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:15,720
With this remarkable technology, DMA provides multi-purpose, volumetric, 3D visualization systems for use, for example, in science, medicine, education, entertainment, and advertising.

143
00:20:15,720 --> 00:20:29,640
As an example of this work, DMA, under contract from DARPA, delivered a 3D real-time virtual reality surgical simulation system targeted for training military surgical units.

144
00:20:29,640 --> 00:20:44,680
Not only will the system provide 3D floating images of human organs, it will also provide tactile and visual feedback to physicians and students as they interact with the images during the surgical simulations.

145
00:20:44,680 --> 00:20:52,200
With these RD efforts, DMA aims to create a new generation of visual technology.

