00:20:57,320 --> 00:21:04,680
Do we want to have for the word hologram or holography, which is the process of creating holograms?

147
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:11,240
Can we say that any any image that is floating in space is a hologram?

148
00:21:11,240 --> 00:21:46,800
Now I know myself, as many of you probably know who have worked with holography, and as many listeners who have never worked with holography at all may know, just from thinking, we get a lot of questions asking about floating images, holograms, and usually we try our best in the most polite way possible to explain that just because an image is floating in space does not necessarily make it a hologram, more than likely not a hologram, and it's another technology that's used to create it.

149
00:21:46,800 --> 00:21:54,160
But do we have to reexamine this and broaden our scope of a hologram or holography?

150
00:21:54,160 --> 00:22:04,720
I went to Graham Saxby's book Practical Holography, and I found the following somewhat definitions of this.

151
00:22:04,720 --> 00:22:23,760
We found that the term hologram was coined in 1948 by Dennis Gabor, with the prefix holo coming from a Greek word meaning whole, and the syllable gram from another Greek word conventionally signifying a drawing or other visual representation.

152
00:22:23,760 --> 00:22:27,120
The term holography was coined by G.

153
00:22:27,280 --> 00:22:27,600
L.

154
00:22:27,600 --> 00:22:30,080
Rogers, and I've tried to find some information on G.

155
00:22:30,080 --> 00:22:30,320
L.

156
00:22:30,320 --> 00:22:36,880
Rogers on the uh on the net, and I have not turned up anything, so I will continue to look into that.

157
00:22:36,880 --> 00:22:41,520
It also goes on to say that a holograph is a document that is in the author's handwriting.

158
00:22:41,520 --> 00:22:49,040
Although the Oxford English Dictionary does accept holograph as an alternative to hologram.

159
00:22:49,040 --> 00:23:04,120
To the physicist, a hologram is a record of the interference of two beams of coherent light, which are mutually correlated in the form of a microscopic pattern of interference fringes.

160
00:23:04,120 --> 00:23:18,440
To the informed layperson, it is a photographic film or plate which has been exposed to laser light and processed in such a way that when illuminated properly, it produces a three-dimensional image.

161
00:23:18,440 --> 00:23:26,920
Less well informed people often seem to think of a hologram simply as some sort of three-dimensional photograph.

162
00:23:26,920 --> 00:23:49,400
Now to summarize this, we go on to read a hologram is a complete record of the information, and when correctly illuminated, it will generate a replica of the object wavefront, enabling the viewer to see an image which in every respect replicates the object with full parallax.

163
00:23:49,400 --> 00:23:56,200
I think one of the most important things through all this to keep in mind is this.

164
00:23:56,200 --> 00:24:08,760
A hologram is a record of the interference of two beams of coherent light which are mutually co-related in the form of a microscopic pattern of interference fringes.

165
00:24:23,480 --> 00:24:28,040
The one that I want to refer to here, actually I pulled three of them.

